# L0 / B010 — security-scan (+layers), swagger, template-maintenance, verify.

C R208 OL WF-020 | MUST | Security review is evidence-based: report concrete risks in the context of actual exposure, distinguish confirmed findings from items needing verification (NEEDS VERIFICATION), assign severity from exploitability, reachability, impact and context (never mechanically from a pattern, CVSS or OWASP category), do not suppress a real secret because it sits in a Development file, name workflows needing threat modeling instead of claiming the scan proves them secure, and never invent exploitability. | security review | none stated
C R209 OL WF-004 | MUST | Verification starts by reviewing the final changed-file set and diff: confirm scope (no accidental unrelated refactoring), no generated/build artifacts, secrets or environment-specific credentials, temporary diagnostics removed only after their uniquely verified behavior is preserved; determine the affected areas before choosing checks; after fixes review the final diff again (unrelated edits, commented-out code, temporary logging, TODO/FIXME, stale temporary tests, architecture drift, unapproved drift from product inputs, stale surfaces after a settings change). | verification | none stated
C R210 OL WF-005 | MUST | Build the affected backend solution/projects and the frontend with its configured script; a build failure means the implementation is not complete; run relevant tests (whole suite for small solutions, affected projects first for large ones) and investigate every newly failing relevant test. | verification | none stated
C R211 OL WF-006 | DEFAULT | For a new runnable application or substantial startup, configuration, persistence or full-stack changes verify the intended Development startup and key composition surfaces (host starts, endpoint reachable, Swagger UI loads, configuration binds, database initialization succeeds, frontend dev server starts, API base URL and CORS compatible); a successful build alone does not prove runtime composition. | verification | none stated
C R212 OL RUN-010 | MUST (IDE0005 surfaced in build) | For every C# file created or modified by the task remove unused or redundant using directives (including those already provided by implicit/global usings unless needed for clarity or disambiguation), verify the changed files themselves, and do not perform an unrelated repository-wide cleanup. | changed C# files | Imports kept for clarity or disambiguation.
C X24 EX WF-020,WF-009 | MUST | Security-scan report shape: every report states the static-analysis limitation; severity uses the five levels Critical (sparingly) / High / Medium / Low / Info; each confirmed finding gives severity, file and location, title, evidence, why it is a risk, likely impact, smallest remediation and OWASP category when applicable; the report contains scope, limitations, a severity summary, findings and per-layer results. | security reviews | none stated | WF-020 requires evidence-based contextual severity and WF-009 truthful status reporting; the oracle prescribes no report structure, severity scale or mandatory limitation statement. | A security review delivered without the limitation statement or the per-layer table does not follow the procedure.
C X25 EX - | MUST | template-maintenance runs only when the user invokes it (disable-model-invocation; never started automatically), and maintenance keeps the always-loaded surface compact (CLAUDE.md plus the two imported decision summaries; the checker prints its estimate). | instruction-system maintenance | none stated | Invocation and loading-surface rules of the template; no oracle policy regulates how the instruction system is maintained. | The agent may not start template-maintenance on its own initiative, and moving path rules into the always-loaded surface violates the procedure.

